The semi-automated mailing of the PC binaries seems to be progressing
without any problems.  Those of you who requested that the binaries
be mailed to you should receive overnight.  (The mailer runs only
at night).  If you have a problem with a bad file, send a note
requesting that the messed up file be resent.

For reasons beyond human understanding some files travel faster than
others, rest assured that one of the first few files you recieve
will contain instructions.

For those of you who missed the original posting, you can request
a copy of the latest binaries by mailing a letter to the following
address:

wizard@chemstor.uoregon.edu

And include your address on the first like like so:

SEND PCNH307 yourname@your.address
 
You can also send comments or questions to the same address.

If you have ftp capability, it would be helpful if you picked up
the binaries yourself.  Try the /pub/NH3.0/PC directory on
linc.cis.upenn.edu.

For the PC team

Kevins@cie.uoregon.edu


